coder › Implemented debounce in `src/debounce.ts` and added tests in `src/debounce.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `debounce(fn, ms, timers)` validates `ms < 0` with `RangeError`, then keeps `handle`/`lastArgs` state. Each call stores the latest args, clears any pending timer via `timers.clearTimeout`, and schedules `run` via `timers.setTimeout(run, ms)`.
- `cancel()` clears the pending timer (if any) and drops stored args.
- `flush()` clears the pending timer and invokes `fn` immediately with the latest args; no-op when nothing is pending.
- Defaults `timers` to the global `setTimeout`/`clearTimeout` wrapper, so injected fake timers control time in tests.
- Tests use a small fake-timer harness (`setTimeout`/`clearTimeout` + `advance`) covering: trailing call with latest args, timer reset on rapid calls, `ms` passthrough, `cancel` (pending and idle), `flush` (pending runs once and cancels timer, idle no-op), `RangeError` on negative `ms`, and default global timers via `Bun.sleep`.

